.TH auto-adduser 8

\" auto-man2man (used in generating subcommand lists) depends on this section
.SH NAME
.PP
auto-adduser - Interactively add a user

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-adduser [username]
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
username    Optional username for the new user
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-adduser
command interactively adds a new user to the system, prompting for all
essential user information (username, primary group name, UID, GID,
etc.).
In addition to collecting basic user information stored in /etc/passwd,
.B auto-adduser
performs the following functions:

o Supports retrieving user information from LDAP or AD servers.

o Prompts to add the new user to OS-specific special groups such as
wheel, operator, video (FreeBSD), and _shutdown (OpenBSD).

o Prompts to add the new user to additional supplementary groups.

o Prompts to set the new user's login class (BSD), which determines
user limits, default path, localization, umask, etc.

This ensures that the user account is fully configured for the user's
role on the system, without requiring any additional steps.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-adduser
.ad
.fi

.SH FILES
.nf
.na
/etc/passwd, /etc/group, /etc/login.conf (BSD), ldap.conf
.ad
.fi

